<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1 (desert sheet slug
  `filter-feeding-shade-whale-megafauna-body-donor-gr-paraceram`).
  desert.md §4c/§10's whale-metaphor megafauna: "they filter-feed through the
  sand, straining the buried canopy and the small life grazing it... a
  megafauna IS a mobile shade patch — the only one that exists." The desert
  roster (`rosters/desert.json` "new_defs") names the body donor as
  `GR_Paraceramuffalo` (Vanilla Genetics Expanded, bodySize 16) but flags it
  "RESKIN SOURCE ONLY, GR_ defs never placed as-is" — VGE is a "dormant"
  donor in this campaign's fauna census
  (`design/Jawa/fauna/animal_census.csv`), not a live dependency, so its
  texPath is not reused here.

  Reskinned instead from `RSW_Horax` (already-ported, "ours"-status donor,
  same RSW mod, baseBodySize 15 — close enough to the sheet's bs16 target to
  reuse body/art verbatim, exactly the RSW_WraidAlpha/RSW_Wraid precedent
  from DESERT_BURST_PREDATOR_FLAGSHIP_1: same body, same texPath, a tint to
  differentiate, zero new PNGs). `desert.json`'s fauna roster already carries
  `Horax` as the desert's own placeholder for this megafauna band ("interim
  ... positional megafauna until the shade-whale def lands") — RSW_Horax
  stays wired in RUT_Desert.xml as its own entry (not removed, same
  precedent), this def is the flagship it was standing in for.

  Re-purposed from Horax's predator profile to the sheet's actual megafauna
  role: herbivore/filter-feeder (not carnivore), solitary (not territorial
  predator), calm (low manhunter chances) — "a mobile shade patch", not a
  monster. Live birth instead of Horax's egg-laying: "whale-metaphor" reads
  as mammal, and it drops the need for new egg art.

  Shade-seeking wander is wired for real via `RM_ShadeSeekingWanderExtension`
  (DESERT_SHADE_GRID_KEYSTONE_1, RM_CreatureBehaviors) — existing C#
  infrastructure, zero new code, and per that extension's own source comment
  the intended first consumer. This covers "they absorb enormous heat on the
  crossing and radiate it fiercely once shade is reached" as an actual
  in-game behaviour, not just prose.

  DESERT_SHADE_WHALE_FILTERFEED_1 landed §4c's two defining mechanics on this
  def as the second wave `desert.json`'s "def can land first" note anticipated
  — sand filter-feeding (RM_FilterFeedExtension, below) and dung-seeding
  (RM_CompProperties_DungSeeder, below), both new C# in RM_CreatureBehaviors
  alongside the shade grid they read. Each carries its own Mod Settings toggle
  and rate dial ("Filter-feeding from the ground", "Dung seeding at shade
  patches"). See those two blocks for the numbers and why each was chosen.

  FILTH_ON_NATURAL_TERRAIN_NOOP_1 (2026-09-21): both mechanics' filth def was
  Core's Filth_AnimalFilth, which can never place on Sand/SoftSand — its
  placementMask is [Terrain]-only and NaturalTerrainBase's
  filthAcceptanceMask is [Unnatural]-only, confirmed with 6 filter-feed
  bouts and 8 dung events on live Sand producing 0 filth. Both fields now
  point at this mod's own RSW_Filth_WhaleDung (RSW_Filth_WhaleDung.xml),
  same look, placementMask [Unnatural] — the mask Sand/SoftSand actually
  accept. See that def's header for the full engine finding.

  Working name only, same status as `staggerseed` and `glitter-birds` in
  desert.md's own Owed section — "shade whale" is descriptive, not an
  owner-given name.
-->
<Defs>

<!-- ThingDef -->
<ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase" ADogSaidBody="LegsTail">
    <defName>RSW_ShadeWhale</defName>
    <label>shade whale</label>
    <description>A colossal, slow-moving grazer that crosses the open dayside in a single committed march, absorbing a furnace's worth of heat along the way. It filter-feeds through the sand as it goes, straining the buried canopy and the small life sheltering in it, and radiates the crossing's heat fiercely once it reaches shade — which is also the only moving shadow most of this desert ever sees. Nothing this large has a predator. Everything that can reach it rides in its shadow instead.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>2.2</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>6000</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>95</ComfyTemperatureMax>
      <FilthRate>24</FilthRate>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.55</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.60</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>0.70</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Wildness>0.9</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>left foot</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>16</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.0</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>RSW_SWLeftHoof</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>right foot</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>16</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.0</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>RSW_SWRightHoof</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>spiked club-tail</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Blunt</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>18</power>
        <cooldownTime>2.6</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>RSW_SWTailAttackTool</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
        <chanceFactor>0.3</chanceFactor>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- DESERT_SHADE_GRID_KEYSTONE_1's shade-seeking wander insert — steers
           idle wandering toward RM_MapComponent_ShadeGrid.ShadeAt cells
           instead of a uniform-random destination. Existing infrastructure,
           first real consumer. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_ShadeSeekingWanderExtension">
        <minShadeToPrefer>0.5</minShadeToPrefer>
      </li>
      <!-- DESERT_SHADE_WHALE_FILTERFEED_1. desert.md §4c: "They filter-feed
           through the sand, straining the buried canopy and the small life
           grazing it. Anything that slow needs food that cannot run."
           §10's table says the route has to be C# because FoodTypeFlags is a
           closed enum with no terrain member; RM_JobGiver_FilterFeedTerrain +
           RM_JobDriver_FilterFeedTerrain are that route, and they satisfy
           Need_Food directly rather than ingesting a Thing.

           Sand and SoftSand only. Gravel, the patch floors and every built
           floor are excluded on purpose: the buried canopy it strains is the
           ultracactus (RSW_Ultracactus, fertilityMin 0.05 "so it takes Sand"),
           and open sand is the one ground in this biome the ultracactus owns
           uncontested. A whale standing on a colony floor is a whale that has
           to eat like everything else.

           Numbers, chosen here rather than specified by the item:
           - beginBelowFoodPercent 0.75 — well above vanilla's hungry
             threshold, because §4c's animal grazes continuously AS IT
             CROSSES, not in trips once it is starving.
           - foodPercentPerBout 0.10 / boutDurationTicks 1200 (20 s) — sand is
             thin food. Ten slow bouts to fill from empty is the mechanical
             form of "anything that slow needs food that cannot run"; it also
             keeps the whale parked and grazing for long stretches, which is
             what makes it a MOBILE SHADE PATCH other creatures can use.
           - searchRadius 20 — a bodySize-16 animal committing to a walk. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_FilterFeedExtension">
        <feedTerrainDefNames>
          <li>Sand</li>
          <li>SoftSand</li>
        </feedTerrainDefNames>
        <beginBelowFoodPercent>0.75</beginBelowFoodPercent>
        <foodPercentPerBout>0.10</foodPercentPerBout>
        <boutDurationTicks>1200</boutDurationTicks>
        <searchRadius>20</searchRadius>
        <!-- FILTH_ON_NATURAL_TERRAIN_NOOP_1: RSW_Filth_WhaleDung, not Core's
             Filth_AnimalFilth — Filth_AnimalFilth's placementMask is
             [Terrain]-only, and Sand/SoftSand (NaturalTerrainBase) accept
             only [Unnatural], so every leavings drop here was a silent
             no-op. See RSW_Filth_WhaleDung.xml's own header for the full
             engine finding; do not swap this back to Filth_AnimalFilth. -->
        <leavingsFilthDef>RSW_Filth_WhaleDung</leavingsFilthDef>
        <leavingsFilthCount>1</leavingsFilthCount>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <comps>
      <!-- DESERT_SHADE_WHALE_FILTERFEED_1. desert.md §4c: "They leave massive
           dung at shade patches, and that dung immediately seeds young plants
           and young creatures around it. So the megafauna are the biome's
           circulatory system — the only long-distance vector, carrying seeds,
           riders and parasites between patch-networks that are otherwise
           sealed from each other, and fertilising every harbour they stop at."

           Gated on RM_MapComponent_ShadeGrid.ShadeAt, so a dung drop out on
           the open crossing leaves filth and nothing else, and only a stop in
           a harbour actually fertilises it. That gate is the mechanic: it is
           what makes this animal a vector BETWEEN patches rather than a
           fertiliser spreader over sand.

           Numbers, chosen here rather than specified by the item:
           - intervalTicksRange 15000~30000 (6–12 in-game hours) — a stop, not
             a trickle. §4c says "massive dung", once in a while.
           - minShadeToSeed 0.35 — below the 0.5 its own shade-seeking wander
             prefers, so a whale that settled for a thinner shadow than it
             wanted still fertilises it.
           - seedPlants RSW_Ultracactus — the buried canopy it strains is also
             what it carries. The comp would otherwise fall back to the map
             biome's own wild plants; naming it here keeps the desert's
             circulatory system closed on itself, and the ultracactus is the
             one desert plant whose own fertilityMin lets it take the sand a
             whale stops on.
           - wildlifeSpawnChance 0.15, maxWildlifeBodySize 0.6 — "young
             creatures", the riders and parasites, drawn from whatever the map
             biome already spawns small. Roughly one arrival per two to three
             days of a whale resting in shade, which is a visible event rather
             than a population source. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_CompProperties_DungSeeder">
        <intervalTicksRange>15000~30000</intervalTicksRange>
        <minShadeToSeed>0.35</minShadeToSeed>
        <!-- FILTH_ON_NATURAL_TERRAIN_NOOP_1: same swap as leavingsFilthDef
             above, same reason — RSW_Filth_WhaleDung.xml. -->
        <dungFilthDef>RSW_Filth_WhaleDung</dungFilthDef>
        <dungFilthCount>4</dungFilthCount>
        <seedRadius>5.9</seedRadius>
        <growthBoost>0.25</growthBoost>
        <maxPlantsBoosted>12</maxPlantsBoosted>
        <seedPlants>
          <li>RSW_Ultracactus</li>
        </seedPlants>
        <seedPlantCount>1~3</seedPlantCount>
        <seedPlantGrowth>0.05</seedPlantGrowth>
        <wildlifeSpawnChance>0.15</wildlifeSpawnChance>
        <maxWildlifeBodySize>0.6</maxWildlifeBodySize>
        <seededWildlifeAgeYears>0.4</seededWildlifeAgeYears>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <race>
      <body>RSW_Horax</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal> <!-- solitary — "a megafauna IS a mobile shade patch, the only one that exists" (desert.md §4c) -->
      <baseBodySize>16.0</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>12.0</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>2.2</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <gestationPeriodDays>25</gestationPeriodDays>
      <leatherDef>RSW_Leather_Horax</leatherDef>
      <specificMeatDef>RSW_Saurian_Meat</specificMeatDef>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0.05</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.10</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <nameGenerator>SWAnimalNamerMale</nameGenerator>
      <nameGeneratorFemale>SWAnimalNamerFemale</nameGeneratorFemale>
      <lifeExpectancy>90</lifeExpectancy>
      <wildBiomes>
        <Desert>0.015</Desert>
      </wildBiomes>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.5</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>1.0</minAge>
          <soundWounded>RSW_Pawn_Horax_Wounded</soundWounded>
          <soundDeath>RSW_Pawn_Horax_Death</soundDeath>
          <soundCall>RSW_Pawn_Horax_Call</soundCall>
          <soundAngry>RSW_Pawn_Horax_Angry</soundAngry>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_BigBash_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Herbivore_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
      <li>AnimalFarm</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

<!-- PawnKindDef -->
<PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RSW_ShadeWhale</defName>
    <label>shade whale</label>
    <race>RSW_ShadeWhale</race>
    <combatPower>650</combatPower>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.08</ecoSystemWeight>
    <wildGroupSize>1</wildGroupSize>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>swanimals/Horax/Horax</texPath>
          <color>(178, 148, 104)</color> <!-- pale sun-baked ochre/tan, reskin over the shared Horax art — desert.md §9 palette, zero new PNGs -->
          <drawSize>2.2</drawSize>
          <shadowData>
            <volume>(0.4, 0.3, 0.3)</volume>
            <offset>(0,0,-0.2)</offset>
          </shadowData>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>swanimals/Horax/Horax_Dessicated</texPath>
          <drawSize>2.2</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>swanimals/Horax/Horax</texPath>
          <color>(178, 148, 104)</color>
          <drawSize>6.4</drawSize>
          <shadowData>
            <volume>(0.6, 0.45, 0.45)</volume>
            <offset>(0,0,-0.25)</offset>
          </shadowData>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>swanimals/Horax/Horax_Dessicated</texPath>
          <drawSize>6.4</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>swanimals/Horax/Horax</texPath>
          <color>(178, 148, 104)</color>
          <drawSize>8.8</drawSize>
          <shadowData>
            <volume>(0.8, 0.6, 0.6)</volume>
            <offset>(0,0,-0.3)</offset>
          </shadowData>
        </bodyGraphicData>
        <dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>swanimals/Horax/Horax_Dessicated</texPath>
          <drawSize>8.8</drawSize>
        </dessicatedBodyGraphicData>
      </li>
